<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36694" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plōrātus</span></b> ,
		ūs, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				wailing</i>, <i>weeping</i>, <i>lamenting.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virginalem ploratum edere, Cic. poët.
					Tusc. 2, 9, 21: ploratum infantis cohibere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					36, 5, 4, § 29</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vox ploratūs,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Matt. 2, 18</span></i>
			.—In plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnia mulierum ploratibus sonant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					29, 17</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, of the <i>weeping</i>
			or <i>bleeding</i> of a tree, <i><span class="en">Plin. 12,
				25, 54, § 116</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
